A||N||1||86SEFIERO||removing rear glass ||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||06-15-2000||03:44 AM||||<BR>whats the easiest way to remove rear window out of car and not breaking it at the same time? I have a parts car and I would like to remove the glass with rear defroster before I ship it to the boneyard just incase mine gets broken.||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||06-15-2000||07:52 AM||||    You have to remove all the interior and exterior trim around the window. Start with a small from the inside and work a hole through the bottom and the top of the window near one edge, use a very small screw driver or some other pointed object to work through the weather seal. use a piece of piano wire or guitar string and run it through the top and the bottom hole. Go out side the vehical and work the wire back and forth toward the other edge, being carefull of the defroster wiring. Oh yeah, it's not a fun job and you'll need plenty of patience. Good luck!<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
